---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Contact"
  metaTitle="Contact"
  description="How to report a formula error, an accessibility barrier or a security issue. No contact form, because the site has no server to receive one."
  path="/contact"
  lastUpdated="2026-08-20"
  keywords={['contact']}
>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="rounded-md border border-caution/40 bg-caution-surface p-3 text-xs text-caution">
    <strong>Owner placeholder.</strong> Replace the contact address in <code
      >src/config/site.ts</code
    >
    before launch. It appears here, in the privacy policy, in the terms and in security.txt, and changing
    it in that one file updates all of them.
  </p>

  <h2>Why there is no contact form</h2>

  <p>
    A form needs somewhere to send the submission, which means a server, which means somewhere your
    message is stored and something else to secure. This site is static files with no backend, and
    keeping it that way is the reason nothing you type into a calculator can leave your device. An
    email address is a fair trade for that.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a formula error</h2>

  <p>
    These are the most useful reports we get, and they are taken seriously. Please include the page,
    the inputs you used, the result you got and the result you expected — and a source if you have
    one. A citation to the original paper makes a correction quick and certain.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every formula is checked against worked examples from its source in an automated test suite, so
    a genuine discrepancy usually means either a transcription error worth fixing everywhere, or a
    standard that has been superseded since the page was written. Both matter.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting an accessibility barrier</h2>

  <p>
    Tell us which page, what you were trying to do, and what browser and assistive technology you
    were using if you are comfortable sharing it. See the
    <a href="/accessibility/">accessibility statement</a> for what is already known to fall short. These
    are treated as defects, not feature requests.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting a security issue</h2>

  <p>
    Please report privately in the first instance, following
    <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>. Testing against this site is welcome
    within the scope described there; please do not run automated scanning that places load on the
    host.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cannot help with</h2>

  <p>
    We cannot give personal health, nutrition or training advice, interpret your results, or tell
    you what you should weigh or eat. That is not modesty — an equation and a web page do not know
    enough about you to answer those questions responsibly. A doctor or a qualified professional
    does.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you have concerns about eating, weight or body image, please take them to someone qualified
    to help rather than to a calculator.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
